The TypeScript engine under src/meat/ and the ported CLI modules (src/cli/main.ts,
cache.ts, render.ts, stdin.ts) were ported from the upstream Go implementation
and then modified and extended: the product and commands were renamed to
columbo, workflow subcommands (prime, status, snapshot, record, setup,
capabilities, guide), local Git-backed state records, project skill
installation, and additional platform support were added. The upstream Go
sources remain under meat/ and cmd/ as a reference implementation.

columbo-review is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored
by, or endorsed by Bold Software, Inc. "meat" is used only to describe
compatibility with the upstream format.
